<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 6 October, from 23 to 1981.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">23</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rebels kill Wang Mang as Chang'an falls</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebel forces broke into Chang'an and killed Wang Mang, the usurper who had founded the Xin dynasty. His death cleared the way for the restoration of the Han dynasty under Emperor Guangwu.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1600</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peri's Euridice, the oldest surviving opera, is performed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jacopo Peri's Euridice was staged at the Pitti Palace in Florence during celebrations for the marriage of Maria de' Medici to Henry IV of France. It is the earliest opera whose music survives complete.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1927</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Jazz Singer premieres in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Warner Bros released The Jazz Singer, starring Al Jolson, the first feature film with synchronised dialogue and singing. Its success ended the silent era within a few years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1973</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Egypt and Syria attack Israel on Yom Kippur</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Egyptian and Syrian forces launched surprise attacks on Israeli positions in Sinai and the Golan Heights on the holiest day of the Jewish year. The war ended in Israeli counter-offensives and reshaped Middle Eastern diplomacy.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1981</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Egyptian president Anwar Sadat is assassinated</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Islamist army officers shot Anwar Sadat during a military parade in Cairo marking the 1973 war. Sadat had signed a peace treaty with Israel in 1979 and shared the Nobel Peace Prize with Menachem Begin.</p></li></ol>
